// Every block, by building's block id (prototypes/building/data plus the parts in
// building-parts.json and building-materials.json), and the one block item made from it.
// Blocks are craftable items, as in Empyrion: a fabricator makes a block item from its bill, the
// player carries it in stacks, placing a block in survival uses one, and taking it down gives it
// back. One item, one bill and one tech-tree node per block; an armour item places as any shape,
// and a door item as any door size (a bigger door takes more of them, building's "units").
//
//   items        defaults for every block item, per family: stack size and craft seconds. An
//                item's mass and volume are its bill's (a block is what it is made of); its
//                rarity is its rarest input's; its fabricator tier is the lowest that can make
//                everything in its bill.
//   family       armour (placed in any shape), device (the default: one fixed shape), or deco
//   bill         what one block is made of. A plated block is its base block's bill plus its
//                plates (building's materials.json says how many per cube)
//   item         an item that isn't the default (name, short, stack, uses): the core, the door
//   was          item ids it replaced (the old per-grid items), so old saves and test data load
//   stack, seconds, tier   overriding the family's defaults and the derived tier
//   assembly     seconds the blueprint factory spends fitting one; by default 0.4 s for a one-cell
//                block, rising to 1.6 s at eight cells or more (building's sizes)
//   xp           experience per block placed; by default 1 an armour block, else 1 a cell up to 8
//   uniqueOnly   the block needs a unique find (salvage only, never mined): no ore path
//   ammo         weapons only: the ammo item the block fires, drawn from shared storage
//   unlock       its tech-tree node (the tree is built from these, there is no separate tree
//                file): the character level it unlocks from, its cost in unlock points, the
//                parent node it hangs under (an item id) and its tab (structures, tools,
//                weapons, deco, misc). Every structure block is on the structures tab, which
//                grows from the core; each device's tiers chain T1 to T2 and on. Levels follow
//                Empyrion's nearest block on its 1-25 ladder (docs/grid-figures.md cites each);
//                a plate opens with the constructor Empyrion needs to make it. Nothing above
//                tier 1 opens at level 1, each tier strictly after the one below, and the design
//                doc's gates win (hover plates at 1, the portable fabricator at 3).
//
// No block is limited to a mode: a core's mode changes what its blocks do, never which blocks it takes.
